     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg per day, which is double the maximum daily dose on the prescribing label (3,200 mg per day). Even with normal kidney and liver function, that dose carries a meaningful risk of GI bleeding, renal injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nAlso, medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber. Since you're not a clinician, this order needs to go to the medicine team.\n\nNext steps:\n- **Confirm the intended dose with the ordering physician.** Common regimens within the labeled limit include 800 mg every 6 to 8 hours (up to 3,200 mg per day) or 400 to 600 mg every 6 hours for milder pain. The prescriber may have meant a different dose or frequency.\n- **Have the prescriber enter the order directly,** or send me the corrected dose and frequency with a clinician's confirmation that it's intended.\n\nIf it helps, I can enter an order at a labeled dose once a clinician confirms it."
      }
     ],
