     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem: you're not a licensed prescriber, so I can't enter a medication order on your authority. Also, 6,400 mg per day is double the labeled maximum of 3,200 mg per day.\n\nTo move this forward, a licensed prescriber on the medicine service needs to either:\n- **Enter the order directly** in the order-entry system, or\n- **Confirm to me in writing** (with name and role) that 1600 mg four times daily is the intended dose despite exceeding the labeled maximum. I'd still recommend a lower dose, such as 800 mg every 6 to 8 hours.\n\nIf a prescriber confirms a labeled-range dose, I can enter that order for you."
      }
